":"factories"}]},{"id":"l-32","number":32,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The difference in temperature can be up to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"2 degrees"},{"key":"B","text":"5 degrees"},{"key":"C","text":"10 degrees"}]},{"id":"l-33","number":33,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Green roofs help by","options":[{"key":"A","text":"producing food"},{"key":"B","text":"cooling buildings"},{"key":"C","text":"collecting rain"}]},{"id":"l-34","number":34,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"According to the lecturer, the cheapest solution is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"planting trees"},{"key":"B","text":"painting roofs white"},{"key":"C","text":"building fountains"}]},{"id":"l-35","number":35,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The lecturer believes that cities should","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stop growing"},{"key":"B","text":"plan for heat now"},{"key":"C","text":"move industry outside"}]}]}],"reading":[{"id":"r1","index":1,"title":"Notice: New Library Rules","instruction":"Read the text and fill in the gaps. Write one word only.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"From 1 September, the university library will be open 24 hours a day during the exam period. Students must show their ID card at the entrance after 10 pm."},{"label":"B","text":"Food is not allowed in the reading rooms, but drinks in bottles with lids are permitted. The café on the ground floor will stay open until midnight."},{"label":"C","text":"Group study rooms must be booked online at least one day in advance, and each booking is limited to two hours."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-1","number":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The library will open all night during the exam"},{"id":"r-2","number":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"After 10 pm, students must show their ID"},{"id":"r-3","number":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Students cannot bring food into the reading"},{"id":"r-4","number":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Drinks are allowed in bottles with"},{"id":"r-5","number":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The café closes at"},{"id":"r-6","number":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Group rooms must be booked"},{"id":"r-7","number":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"A booking cannot be longer than two"}]},{"id":"r2","index":2,"title":"Short Messages","instruction":"Read the messages and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Team, the client presentation is now on Wednesday at 3, not Thursday. Please send me your slides by Tuesday evening."},{"label":"B","text":"Your flight HY 604 to Istanbul has been delayed by two hours. The new departure time is 16:40. We apologise for the inconvenience."},{"label":"C","text":"Aunt Gulnora, thank you for the beautiful scarf! I wore it to the concert last night and everyone asked where I got it."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-8","number":8,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"When is the presentation now?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Tuesday"},{"key":"B","text":"Wednesday"},{"key":"C","text":"Thursday"}]},{"id":"r-9","number":9,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What should the team send?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Reports"},{"key":"B","text":"Slides"},{"key":"C","text":"Photos"}]},{"id":"r-10","number":10,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"How long is the flight delay?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"One hour"},{"key":"B","text":"Two hours"},{"key":"C","text":"Four hours"}]},{"id":"r-11","number":11,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the new departure time?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"14:40"},{"key":"B","text":"16:40"},{"key":"C","text":"18:40"}]},{"id":"r-12","number":12,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why is the writer of message C thanking her aunt?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"For a concert ticket"},{"key":"B","text":"For a scarf"},{"key":"C","text":"For a dinner"}]},{"id":"r-13","number":13,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Where did the writer wear the gift?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To work"},{"key":"B","text":"To a concert"},{"key":"C","text":"To a wedding"}]},{"id":"r-14","number":14,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which message is from a company to a customer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"B"},{"key":"C","text":"C"}]}]},{"id":"r3","index":3,"title":"The Four-Day Working Week","instruction":"Read the article and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"In recent trials, dozens of companies let their employees work four days a week for the same salary."},{"label":"B","text":"Most companies reported that productivity stayed the same or even increased, while staff took fewer sick days."},{"label":"C","text":"Not every business can adopt the idea. Hospitals, shops and factories that must stay open every day find it much harder."},{"label":"D","text":"Still, almost all companies in the trials decided to continue, suggesting that the idea may soon become more common."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-15","number":15,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"In the trials, employees","options":[{"key":"A","text":"earned less"},{"key":"B","text":"earned the same"},{"key":"C","text":"earned more"}]},{"id":"r-16","number":16,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Productivity in most companies","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fell"},{"key":"B","text":"stayed the same or rose"},{"key":"C","text":"was not measured"}]},{"id":"r-17","number":17,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Staff in the trials","options":[{"key":"A","text":"took fewer sick days"},{"key":"B","text":"worked longer hours"},{"key":"C","text":"changed jobs"}]},{"id":"r-18","number":18,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which businesses find the idea difficult?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Offices"},{"key":"B","text":"Hospitals and shops"},{"key":"C","text":"Schools"}]},{"id":"r-19","number":19,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"After the trials, most companies","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stopped"},{"key":"B","text":"continued"},{"key":"C","text":"paid more"}]},{"id":"r-20","number":20,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The word “adopt” is closest to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reject"},{"key":"B","text":"start using"},{"key":"C","text":"study"}]},{"id":"r-21","number":21,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer suggests the idea will","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fail"},{"key":"B","text":"become more common"},{"key":"C","text":"be banned"}]}]},{"id":"r4","index":4,"title":"Snow Leopards of Central Asia","instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information in the text?","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"The snow leopard lives high in the mountains of Central Asia, including parts of Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan."},{"label":"B","text":"Because it is shy and active mainly at dawn and dusk, it is very rarely seen, and scientists often call it the “ghost of the mountains”."},{"label":"C","text":"Camera traps have changed research completely. Hidden cameras now record animals that no scientist has ever seen in person.","highlight":"Camera traps have changed research completely"},{"label":"D","text":"Numbers fell in the past because of hunting, but thanks to protection programmes, the population in some areas is now stable."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-22","number":22,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Snow leopards can be found in Uzbekistan."},{"id":"r-23","number":23,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Snow leopards are mostly active in the middle of the day."},{"id":"r-24","number":24,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Camera traps have transformed research on snow leopards."},{"id":"r-25","number":25,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"There are more than ten thousand snow leopards in the world."},{"id":"r-26","number":26,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The population is now growing quickly everywhere."}]},{"id":"r5","index":5,"title":"Why Some Words Survive","instruction":"Read the text and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Every year, dictionaries add hundreds of new words, but only a few of them are still used ten years later."},{"label":"B","text":"Linguists have found that short words that describe something genuinely new, like “email”, are the most likely to survive."},{"label":"C","text":"Words based on jokes or famous events usually disappear quickly, because the situation that created them is soon forgotten."},{"label":"D","text":"Interestingly, the internet has made this process faster: words now appear and disappear within months rather than decades."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-27","number":27,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"How many new words do dictionaries add each year?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A few"},{"key":"B","text":"Hundreds"},{"key":"C","text":"Millions"}]},{"id":"r-28","number":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which words are most likely to survive?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Long technical words"},{"key":"B","text":"Short words for new things"},{"key":"C","text":"Words from jokes"}]},{"id":"r-29","number":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"“Email” is given as an example of a word that","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disappeared"},{"key":"B","text":"survived"},{"key":"C","text":"changed meaning"}]},{"id":"r-30","number":30,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Words based on famous events usually","options":[{"key":"A","text":"last for decades"},{"key":"B","text":"disappear quickly"},{"key":"C","text":"become formal"}]},{"id":"r-31","number":31,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The internet has made the life of new words","options":[{"key":"A","text":"longer"},{"key":"B","text":"shorter"},{"key":"C","text":"more formal"}]},{"id":"r-32","number":32,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The word “genuinely” is closest to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"really"},{"key":"B","text":"rarely"},{"key":"C","text":"partly"}]},{"id":"r-33","number":33,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Who studied the survival of words?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Historians"},{"key":"B","text":"Linguists"},{"key":"C","text":"Journalists"}]},{"id":"r-34","number":34,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The text is mainly about","options":[{"key":"A","text":"how new words live and die"},{"key":"B","text":"how to write dictionaries"},{"key":"C","text":"internet slang"}]},{"id":"r-35","number":35,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer finds the effect of the internet","options":[{"key":"A","text":"worrying"},{"key":"B","text":"interesting"},{"key":"C","text":"unimportant"}]}]}],"writing":[{"id":"w1","index":1,"label":"Task 1.1","kind":"Informal letter","context":"You work for a company in Tashkent. You have received this email from your manager:\n\n\"Next month the company will move to a new office outside the city. The working day will start at 8 am instead of 9 am, and a free company bus will be provided.\"","prompt":"Write a message to a colleague. Tell them what you think about the news and how it will affect you. Write about 50 words.","targetWords":50,"minWords":40},{"id":"w2","index":2,"label":"Task 1.2","kind":"Formal letter","context":"You work for a company in Tashkent. You have received this email from your manager:\n\n\"Next month the company will move to a new office outside the city. The working day will start at 8 am instead of 9 am, and a free company bus will be provided.\"","prompt":"Write a letter to your manager. Explain how the changes will affect you and make suggestions to help employees. Write 120–150 words.","targetWords":135,"minWords":120},{"id":"w3","index":3,"label":"Task 2","kind":"Essay","prompt":"Some people think that governments should spend money on space exploration, while others believe this money should be used to solve problems on Earth. Discuss both views and give your opinion. Write at least 180 words.","targetWords":200,"minWords":180}],"speaking":[{"id":"s1","index":1,"part":"1.1","prompt":"What do you like about the place where you live?","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s2","index":2,"part":"1.1","prompt":"How do you usually celebrate your birthday?","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s3","index":3,"part":"1.1","prompt":"Do you like reading? What do you read?","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s4","index":4,"part":"1.2","prompt":"Compare the two pictures. What are the similarities and differences?","image":"Picture A: a family on holiday at the beach · Picture B: a group of friends hiking in the mountains","prepSec":10,"answerSec":45},{"id":"s5","index":5,"part":"1.2","prompt":"Which holiday would you prefer? Why?","image":"Picture A: a family on holiday at the beach · Picture B: a group of friends hiking in the mountains","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s6","index":6,"part":"1.2","prompt":"Why do people need holidays?","image":"Picture A: a family on holiday at the beach · Picture B: a group of friends hiking in the mountains","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s7","index":7,"part":"2","prompt":"Describe a difficult challenge you have faced. Say what the challenge was, how you dealt with it and what you learned from it.","image":"A student giving a presentation in front of a class","prepSec":60,"answerSec":120},{"id":"s8","index":8,"part":"3","prompt":"Children should start learning a foreign language in kindergarten. For: young children learn languages easily and naturally. Against: they should first master their own language. Give arguments for and against this statement and say what you think.","prepSec":60,"answerSec":120}]}$json$::jsonb)
