 to the legend, the discovery was made by","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a farmer"},{"key":"B","text":"a goat herder"},{"key":"C","text":"a king"}]},{"id":"l-33","number":33,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The first coffee houses appeared in","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Europe"},{"key":"B","text":"the Middle East"},{"key":"C","text":"America"}]},{"id":"l-34","number":34,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Coffee houses in Europe were called “penny universities” because people","options":[{"key":"A","text":"studied there"},{"key":"B","text":"discussed ideas"},{"key":"C","text":"paid teachers"}]},{"id":"l-35","number":35,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Today the largest producer of coffee is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Brazil"},{"key":"B","text":"Vietnam"},{"key":"C","text":"Colombia"}]}]}],"reading":[{"id":"r1","index":1,"title":"Notice: Bike Sharing Scheme","instruction":"Read the text and fill in the gaps. Write one word only.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"The city’s new bike sharing scheme starts on 1 May. More than two hundred bikes will be available at thirty stations across the centre."},{"label":"B","text":"To use a bike, download the CityBike app and register with your phone number. The first thirty minutes of every ride are free."},{"label":"C","text":"Bikes must be returned to a station, not left on the street. Riders under sixteen are not allowed to use the service."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-1","number":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The scheme begins in"},{"id":"r-2","number":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Bikes can be found at thirty"},{"id":"r-3","number":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Users must download an"},{"id":"r-4","number":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"To register, you need your phone"},{"id":"r-5","number":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The first half an hour is"},{"id":"r-6","number":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Bikes must not be left on the"},{"id":"r-7","number":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The minimum age is"}]},{"id":"r2","index":2,"title":"Short Messages","instruction":"Read the messages and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Jasur, the plumber is coming at 10 tomorrow to fix the kitchen tap. Can you be at home? I have an early meeting."},{"label":"B","text":"Museum news: from Monday, entry is free for students every Wednesday afternoon. Just show your student card at the desk."},{"label":"C","text":"Hi everyone! Our reunion dinner is moved from the 12th to the 19th because the restaurant is closed. Hope you can still come!"}],"questions":[{"id":"r-8","number":8,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What will the plumber fix?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The shower"},{"key":"B","text":"The kitchen tap"},{"key":"C","text":"The heating"}]},{"id":"r-9","number":9,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why can’t the writer be at home?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"She is travelling"},{"key":"B","text":"She has a meeting"},{"key":"C","text":"She is ill"}]},{"id":"r-10","number":10,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"When is museum entry free for students?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Every Monday"},{"key":"B","text":"Wednesday afternoons"},{"key":"C","text":"At weekends"}]},{"id":"r-11","number":11,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What must students show?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A ticket"},{"key":"B","text":"A student card"},{"key":"C","text":"A passport"}]},{"id":"r-12","number":12,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the new date of the dinner?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The 12th"},{"key":"B","text":"The 19th"},{"key":"C","text":"The 21st"}]},{"id":"r-13","number":13,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why was the dinner moved?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The restaurant is closed"},{"key":"B","text":"People are busy"},{"key":"C","text":"It is a holiday"}]},{"id":"r-14","number":14,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which message gives information to the public?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"B"},{"key":"C","text":"C"}]}]},{"id":"r3","index":3,"title":"The Rise of Audiobooks","instruction":"Read the article and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Audiobooks are more popular than ever. In the last five years, the number of people listening to them has almost tripled."},{"label":"B","text":"Many listeners say audiobooks let them “read” while doing other things, such as driving, cooking or exercising."},{"label":"C","text":"Some teachers worry that listening is not the same as reading. However, studies show that people understand stories equally well in both forms."},{"label":"D","text":"Publishers now hire famous actors to record books, turning a simple reading into a real performance."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-15","number":15,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The number of audiobook listeners has","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doubled"},{"key":"B","text":"almost tripled"},{"key":"C","text":"fallen"}]},{"id":"r-16","number":16,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"People like audiobooks because they can","options":[{"key":"A","text":"learn faster"},{"key":"B","text":"do other things at the same time"},{"key":"C","text":"save money"}]},{"id":"r-17","number":17,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Some teachers are concerned that","options":[{"key":"A","text":"audiobooks are expensive"},{"key":"B","text":"listening differs from reading"},{"key":"C","text":"children stop studying"}]},{"id":"r-18","number":18,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Studies show that understanding of stories is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"better with reading"},{"key":"B","text":"better with listening"},{"key":"C","text":"the same"}]},{"id":"r-19","number":19,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Publishers now use","options":[{"key":"A","text":"computer voices"},{"key":"B","text":"famous actors"},{"key":"C","text":"authors only"}]},{"id":"r-20","number":20,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The word “performance” refers to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a show"},{"key":"B","text":"a test"},{"key":"C","text":"a sale"}]},{"id":"r-21","number":21,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer’s attitude to audiobooks is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"negative"},{"key":"B","text":"positive"},{"key":"C","text":"worried"}]}]},{"id":"r4","index":4,"title":"Tashkent Metro: An Underground Museum","instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information in the text?","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Opened in 1977, the Tashkent Metro was the first underground railway in Central Asia."},{"label":"B","text":"Each station has its own design, with marble walls, chandeliers and mosaics that tell stories about the history and culture of Uzbekistan."},{"label":"C","text":"For many years, taking photographs in the metro was forbidden. The ban was lifted in 2018, and the stations quickly became popular on social media.","highlight":"The ban was lifted in 2018"},{"label":"D","text":"Today the network continues to grow, with new lines connecting the city centre to its outer districts."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-22","number":22,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The Tashkent Metro opened in the 1970s."},{"id":"r-23","number":23,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"All metro stations look the same."},{"id":"r-24","number":24,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Photography in the metro is still banned."},{"id":"r-25","number":25,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The metro carries more than a million passengers a day."},{"id":"r-26","number":26,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"New metro lines are being built."}]},{"id":"r5","index":5,"title":"The Truth About Multitasking","instruction":"Read the text and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Many people are proud of their ability to multitask, answering messages while working or studying."},{"label":"B","text":"Research shows, however, that the brain cannot focus on two demanding tasks at once. Instead, it switches quickly between them."},{"label":"C","text":"Each switch costs time and energy. People who multitask make up to fifty percent more mistakes and take longer to finish."},{"label":"D","text":"Experts recommend “single-tasking”: working on one task for a set period, for example twenty-five minutes, before taking a short break."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-27","number":27,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Many people believe multitasking is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impossible"},{"key":"B","text":"a useful skill"},{"key":"C","text":"dangerous"}]},{"id":"r-28","number":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"According to research, the brain","options":[{"key":"A","text":"does two tasks at once"},{"key":"B","text":"switches between tasks"},{"key":"C","text":"stops working"}]},{"id":"r-29","number":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Switching between tasks costs","options":[{"key":"A","text":"money"},{"key":"B","text":"time and energy"},{"key":"C","text":"nothing"}]},{"id":"r-30","number":30,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"People who multitask make up to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"15% more mistakes"},{"key":"B","text":"25% more mistakes"},{"key":"C","text":"50% more mistakes"}]},{"id":"r-31","number":31,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Experts suggest working on one task for","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ten minutes"},{"key":"B","text":"twenty-five minutes"},{"key":"C","text":"two hours"}]},{"id":"r-32","number":32,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The word “demanding” is closest to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"easy"},{"key":"B","text":"difficult"},{"key":"C","text":"boring"}]},{"id":"r-33","number":33,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Paragraph D gives","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a warning"},{"key":"B","text":"a recommendation"},{"key":"C","text":"a history"}]},{"id":"r-34","number":34,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The text mainly shows that multitasking","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is effective"},{"key":"B","text":"is less effective than people think"},{"key":"C","text":"is a new trend"}]},{"id":"r-35","number":35,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"A student preparing for an exam should","options":[{"key":"A","text":"answer messages while studying"},{"key":"B","text":"focus on one task at a time"},{"key":"C","text":"study without breaks"}]}]}],"writing":[{"id":"w1","index":1,"label":"Task 1.1","kind":"Informal letter","context":"You live in a block of flats. You have received this notice from the building management:\n\n\"From next month, the children’s playground behind the building will be replaced by a car park for residents.\"","prompt":"Write a message to a neighbour who has young children. Tell them about the notice and how you feel about it. Write about 50 words.","targetWords":50,"minWords":40},{"id":"w2","index":2,"label":"Task 1.2","kind":"Formal letter","context":"You live in a block of flats. You have received this notice from the building management:\n\n\"From next month, the children’s playground behind the building will be replaced by a car park for residents.\"","prompt":"Write a letter to the building management. Explain your opinion about the plan and suggest an alternative. Write 120–150 words.","targetWords":135,"minWords":120},{"id":"w3","index":3,"label":"Task 2","kind":"Essay","prompt":"Some people believe that students should be allowed to choose all the subjects they study at school. Others think that schools should decide. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Write at least 180 words.","targetWords":200,"minWords":180}],"speaking":[{"id":"s1","index":1,"part":"1.1","prompt":"What is your favourite season, and why?","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s2","index":2,"part":"1.1","prompt":"How often do you use the internet, and what for?","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s3","index":3,"part":"1.1","prompt":"Tell me about your best friend.","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s4","index":4,"part":"1.2","prompt":"Compare the two pictures. What are the similarities and differences?","image":"Picture A: people shopping online at home · Picture B: people shopping in a busy shopping centre","prepSec":10,"answerSec":45},{"id":"s5","index":5,"part":"1.2","prompt":"Which way of shopping do you prefer? Why?","image":"Picture A: people shopping online at home · Picture B: people shopping in a busy shopping centre","prepSec":5,"answerSec":30},{"id":"s6","index":6,"part":"1.2","prompt":"What are the risks of shopping online?","image":"Picture A: people shopping online 